  {
    "surah_number": 25,
    "ayah_number": 20,
    "surah_name": "Furqan",
    "ayah_translation": "And We did not send before you, [O Muhammad], except men to whom We revealed. So ask the people of remembrance if you do not know. And We did not make them [the prophets] bodies that did not eat food, nor were they immortal. Then We fulfilled for them the promise, and We saved whom We willed and destroyed the transgressors. O you who have been given the Book, believe in what We revealed [to Muhammad] confirming that which is with you before We obliterate [some] faces and turn them toward their backs or curse them as We cursed the companions of the Sabbath. And ever is the command of Allah a predetermined decree. Indeed, Allah does not forgive association of partners with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And whoever associates partners with Allah has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin. Have you not considered those who purify themselves? Rather, Allah purifies whom He wills, and injustice is not done to them, [even] as much as a speck [within a date seed]. Look how they invent about Allah falsehood, and that is sufficient sin for them. Have you not considered those who were given a portion of the Scripture, [but] they believe in idols and false gods and say of those who disbelieve, \"These are better guided than those who believe in the Quran.\" It is those whom Allah has cursed, and he whom Allah curses - you will not find for him a helper. Or have they obtained a share of the kingdom? Then they would not give the people [even] the speck on a date seed. Or do they envy people for what Allah has given them of His bounty? But we had already given the family of Abraham the Scripture and wisdom and conferred upon them a great kingdom. And among them was he who believed in him, and among them was he who turned away from him. And sufficient for them is Hellfire. Indeed, those who disbelieve in Our signs - We will drive them into a fire. Every time their skins are roasted - We will replace them with other skins so they may taste the punishment. Indeed, Allah is ever Exalted and Wise. But those who believed and did righteous deeds - We will admit them to gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding eternally therein, with the permission of Allah. Their greeting therein will be \"Peace.\" Have you not seen how Allah presents an example, [saying], \"How has Allah compared a word [of truth]? It is like a tree with a strong root whose branches extend into the sky\"? It yields its fruit all the time, by permission of its Lord. And Allah presents examples for the people that they might be reminded. And the example of a bad word is like a bad tree, uprooted from the surface of the earth, having no stability. Allah will hold firm those who believe, with the firm word, during worldly life and in the Hereafter. And Allah causes to stray whom He wills and guides whom He wills. And indeed, the wrongdoers are [destined] for a painful punishment. And they will not have been harmed by Allah in anything. Indeed, He is the Most High, the Wise. And they will say, \"Praise to Allah, who has fulfilled His promise to us and made us inheritors of the land [which] we will occupy from Paradise. And excellent is the reward of the workers.\" And you will see the angels surrounding the Throne, praising their Lord with the praise of Him. And it will be judged between them in truth, and it will be said, \"Praise to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\"",
